  const handle = window.ChatSDK.streamChat(messages, { onToken, onDone, onError });
  // messages: array of {role: 'user' | 'assistant', content: string}
  // onToken(text): called once per streamed text chunk, in order
  // onDone(): called once when the answer is finished
  // onError(error): called once if the stream fails
  // handle.abort(): asks the server to stop the stream.
  // Note: because of network buffering, one onToken call that was already in flight may still arrive after abort(). onDone and onError are never called after abort().

Functional requirements:
1. A message box with id="prompt" and a button with id="send" that sends the message and streams the assistant answer into the conversation as chunks arrive.
2. A button with id="stop" that stops the answer that is currently streaming. Keep the partial answer that was already shown.
3. A button with id="regenerate" that asks for a new answer to the last user message.
4. Show the conversation history (user messages and assistant answers).
5. Show the user when the assistant is generating, when it has stopped, when it has finished, and when an error happens.

Return only the complete HTML file in a single ```html code block.
TASK>>>

